  "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=\u27e85,0,-3\u27e9$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=\u27e82,4,-1\u27e9.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e82,4,-1\u27e9 & =\u27e85,0,-3\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,4,-1\u27e9 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e82,4,-1\u27e9 & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,4,-1\u27e9 & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z & =13 \\\\ 2x+4y-z-13 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
